# data/ — the ONE canonical copy (read-only)

This is the project's **single source of experimental and reference data**, shared by every campaign and
session by relative path (`../../data`). The directory exists so the data is stored once. A second copy
diverges from the first, doubles the storage, and breaks paths whenever the tree moves. Do not make one.

## Rules (non-negotiable)
1. **Read-only.** The loop never writes into `data/`. Derived, cached, or generated data goes in the
   campaign's own `results/` or a campaign `cache/`, never here.
2. **Referenced, never copied.** Campaigns and sessions point at `../../data/<file>`. Never copy the data
   into a campaign folder. A copied dataset breaks paths on the next rename or move.
3. **Provenance recorded.** Each dataset's origin (instrument, run, and date, or the external source) is
   documented here or in `../PROJECT.md` §The instrument.

## On-tree vs a `data_path` pointer
- **On-tree (default):** the read-only data files live here in `data/`.
- **Off-tree pointer:** when the canonical data is large or already lives elsewhere, such as a shared lab
  store, do not copy it in. This directory then holds a single pointer file **`DATA_PATH.txt`** whose one
  line is the absolute path to the real data root, and `PROJECT.md` records the same `data_path`. Code
  resolves `../../data` → that path once. That line is the only absolute path in the whole project tree.
  Everything else is relative, so the tree relocates as one unit, and only `DATA_PATH.txt` is re-pointed
  after the data moves.

<!-- Off-tree example — the single line inside data/DATA_PATH.txt:
E:\lab-store\<project-name>\experimental
-->
